module str_ordering.neg_1

// NOVAC_EXPECT dispatches through a protocol
// ONE seeded cause: an ordering of a `str` and an `int`. `str @compare` takes a
// `str`; the pair is no `str` pair, so no `compare` is asked and the operator
// stays refused by the protocol table. The oracle's checker lets the pair
// through and clang refuses the C it emits (registry, filed with sweep 10).
fn main() {
    println("a" < 1)
}
